      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Calumet's German Evangelical Lutheran Church, founded in 1891, offered services in Low German until the mid‑20th century, reflecting the town's heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calumet%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A fire in May 1897 destroyed much of Calumet's downtown, but the community rebuilt quickly, restoring its commercial heart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calumet%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Calumet was incorporated on January 31, 1895, after being first platted in 1887, marking its formal municipal status.",
